# Backend — Flask API

## Structure
- `backend/app/__init__.py` exposes `create_app()` (app factory). No module-level app object.
- Extensions (SQLAlchemy, Migrate, CORS) are created unbound and initialised inside `create_app()`.
- Routes live in Blueprints: `app/api/profiles.py` and `app/api/queries.py`, registered
  under the `/api/v1` prefix.
- Blueprints stay thin: parse/validate input → call a service → serialise output.
  Pipeline logic lives in `app/services/pipeline.py`; scoring math in `app/utils/scoring.py`.

## Endpoints (exactly these; extra ones only after user confirms a spec gap)
```
POST /api/v1/profiles
GET  /api/v1/profiles/<profile_uuid>
POST /api/v1/profiles/<profile_uuid>/run
GET  /api/v1/profiles/<profile_uuid>/queries   ?min_score= &status=visible|not_visible|unknown &page= &per_page=
GET  /api/v1/profiles/<profile_uuid>/recommendations
POST /api/v1/queries/<query_uuid>/recheck
```
- All responses are JSON. No auth layer.
- Validate the `POST /profiles` body: `name`, `domain`, `industry`, `description`,
  `competitors` (list of strings). `domain` matches the frontend validator: bare domain,
  no scheme (`surferseo.com`, not `http://surferseo.com`).
- Validate query params: `min_score` float in 0–1, `status` in the three allowed values,
  `page`/`per_page` positive integers. Invalid values → 400, not a 500.
- Paginated responses include the items plus pagination metadata (page, per_page, total)
  so MatPaginator can render correctly.

## Status codes
- 200 read/update OK · 201 resource created · 400 invalid input/params ·
  404 unknown profile/query UUID · 409 conflicting state · 500 unexpected server error ·
  502 upstream LLM failure that could not be recovered.
- Use exactly one error shape everywhere, produced by registered error handlers:
```json
{ "error": { "code": "not_found", "message": "Profile not found", "details": {} } }
```
- Never return HTML error pages or raw tracebacks. Register JSON handlers for 400/404/405/500.

## CORS & config
- Enable CORS with `flask-cors` for the `/api/*` routes so the Angular app
  (`http://localhost:4200` in dev) can call the API.
- Load config from environment via `python-dotenv`. Variables from the spec:
  `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `DATABASE_URL`, `FLASK_ENV`, `SECRET_KEY`.
- No secrets or keys in code. `backend/.env.example` lists every variable used.
- The API serves on port 5000 (frontend `environment.ts` uses `http://localhost:5000`).
